+# Decision: the lab is the central Scope, and the processes it keeps
+
+Decided by Justin on 4 October 2026, in an afternoon interview. Copied here on 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment
+from `STATE.md` as it stood on 2026-10-04 17:31, the only record of these decisions found in this repository.
+Recording them is not deciding them again, and the wording is `STATE.md`'s.
+
+## Decided
+
+- **The lab is the central Scope** for project management, core issue tracking, code quality and security. Astra is
+  to say what else it should cover.
+- **Where issues live:** a Scope's issues stay in its own repository, on one central map; a `core` label marks a Scope
+  issue that needs ORC's core changed. Later, Scopes may track their own business logic elsewhere.
+- **The processes kept, all of them:**
+  - map and label check;
+  - tests on every PR (orchestrator#144);
+  - the security-review and package-API checks;
+  - daily diary;
+  - weekly adversarial review;
+  - entropy guard at session end;
+  - FRICTION into rules, monthly (orchestrator#60);
+  - branch and worktree cleanup (orchestrator#70);
+  - `/tmp` cleanup (orchestrator#182).
+- **ORC scheduling (orchestrator#166) is built first,** and the scheduled ones run through it.
+- **Astra runs entropy-guard's assessment on ORC and the lab together.** Justin was shaping the brief before it ran.
+- **Moving Stillness is paused:** browser-stack work that touches it (orchestrator#118 and #52, MS #52) waits.
+
+## Waiting
+
+- **Labels:** the type-label proposal waits on Astra's revisions (`reports/2026-10-04-labels-review-astra.md`).
+
+## Held by other records, not copied
+
+`STATE.md` also held decisions whose owner is elsewhere. Justin's 3 October decisions (orchestrator#194 keeps all six
+preview items with a configurable limit and fixed tailnet links; Moving Stillness `failure-verdicts` dropped; MS #52
+reads every entry-list page) belong to those issues and that repository; whether they are recorded there was not
+checked. The 2 October moves to Worktrunk and `gh poi` are recorded in local-config, and to Danger for security
+reviews in ORC's `dangerfile.js` and `AGENTS.md`.
